    "freeTraits": 0,
    "biography": "<h2>Background</h2><p>Embraced in 1235 by Lotharius, Karl Schrekt has spent centuries as one of the Camarilla's most zealous enforcers, having lived through and never forgotten the fires of the Inquisition. He believes the Camarilla is the single most important development in Kindred history and that the Masquerade must be preserved at any cost, recruiting ambitious Kindred from many clans (some say even a bound Setite) to serve as his short-lived, expendable Archons. Rumors swirl endlessly around him &mdash; that he once hunted Kindred, committed diablerie upon a Lupine, even met Caine himself &mdash; but Schrekt confirms nothing. He shares a long, bloody history with Gustav Breidenstein, Prince of East Berlin, and his intervention in Berlin's ongoing succession crisis threatens to destroy whichever prince he judges unworthy. His enhanced Auspex lets him detect lies instantly and communicate telepathically with several people at once; his enhanced Presence lulls listeners into an unnatural, confession-inducing calm.</p><h2>Roleplaying Hints</h2><p>Never smile. Never show fear or anger. Everything about you is hidden from the world. If your best friend were being murdered in front of you, you would casually walk to their assistance. No one gets to you; you are a man of ice.</p>",
    "notes": "Commands a retinue of Archons drawn from multiple clans. Deploys watchers and retainers throughout Berlin to report every violation of Camarilla law. His Blood Bond over the Archon Ramal is described as especially powerful. Convert Disciplines by adding owned power Items (Auspex, Celerity, Dominate, Fortitude, Necromancy, Potence, Presence, Protean, Quietus, and an extensive Thaumaturgy repertoire with numerous Rituals) at Storyteller discretion to match his renowned mastery.",
